==Strategy==
This stage is essentially [[Three Evil Brothers]] reborn, now featuring Deathkory instead of Berserkory as well as metal peons and a Puffzerker. Though Wave Immune units and/or Wave Shields will comprise the majority of your lineup, it is also important to bring an option to delay or prevent Puffzerker from reaching your anti-wave units. Options like [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] and [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Master of Logic Newtone]] fulfill this role, the former also helping to burst down Deathkory quicker as well. Additionally, whenever Koronium is exposed (likely when Deathkory takes a damage knockback), use the thunderbolt cannon and slip in a critical hitter to immediately remove the threat from the stage.

=== Recommended Units ===

* [[Brass Cat]]: One of the most reliable non-uber shield piercers available, Brass can repeatedly take down Deathkory's shield whilst also weakening it for high uptime, extending the lifetime of key units like [[Octopus Cat|Octopus]] in the process.

* [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]]: An alternative to Brass Cat, being about as reliable or somewhat less as a shield piercer but can serve as your critter for Koronium should you need the role compression.

* [[Moneko (Special Cat)|Superstar Moneko]] / [[Backhoe Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Backhoe Cat]]: Both can generate either waves or surges off of Croconators to snipe Koronium before he does anything and juggle Puffzerker. Moneko has a combo to increase the potency of the other critters in your lineup, while Backhoe earns you extra cash.

